# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your values.

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

## Required for Production

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `JWT_SECRET` | Secret key for session tokens (generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | Your production URL (e.g. `https://wills-view.vercel.app`) |
| `TURSO_DATABASE_URL` | Turso/libSQL database URL (required on Vercel — local SQLite cannot persist on serverless) |
| `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` | Turso database auth token |
| `API_URL` | Railway NestJS backend URL (optional — when set, Next.js proxies `/api/*` to this server) |
| `API_HASHKEY` | NewebPay HashKey. **Never commit the real value.** |
| `API_HASHIV` | NewebPay HashIV (paired with HashKey). **Never commit the real value.** |
| `NEWEBPAY_MERCHANT_ID` | NewebPay store ID (e.g. `MS1838384097`) |
| `NEWEBPAY_TEST_MODE` | `true` for sandbox (`ccore.newebpay.com`), `false` for production |

## Backend (Railway)

Set these on your Railway NestJS service:

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `JWT_SECRET` | Must match the frontend `JWT_SECRET` |
| `FRONTEND_URL` | Frontend origin for CORS (e.g. `https://wills-view.vercel.app`) |
| `PORT` | Railway sets this automatically |
| `DATA_DIR` | Persistent volume path for SQLite (e.g. `/data`) |

## Analytics (Optional)

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID` | Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (e.g. `G-XXXXXXXXXX`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN` | Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon token |

## Social Links (Optional)

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_X` | X (Twitter) profile URL (default: `https://x.com`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_LINKEDIN` | LinkedIn page URL (default: `https://www.linkedin.com`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_SLACK` | Slack community URL (default: `https://slack.com/community`) |

## Weekly Articles (Optional)

Automated every Monday via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/weekly-article.yml`).

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | OpenAI API key for article generation (GitHub secret). Without it, a template fallback is used |
| `OPENAI_MODEL` | Model name (default: `gpt-4o-mini`) |

**Manual run:**

```bash
npm run articles:weekly              # generate from latest news
npm run articles:weekly -- --dry-run   # preview without writing files
npm run articles:weekly -- --force     # overwrite if same Monday exists
```

## Demo Accounts

Use these accounts for local development and testing:

- `demo@example.com` / `demo1234` — premium member
- `free@example.com` / `demo1234` — free user (can subscribe via checkout)
